<configs>
<!--
  Armory Unbound - perks.

  A perk is an item_modifier with modifier_tags="auPerk" (corrupted perks: "auPerk,auCorrupted"). The Gunsmith Bench adds
  one to a gun from a perk part; the perk runs at the PART's quality (1-90), never the gun's. A gun holds as many perks as
  it has mod slots, the same perk may go on twice (each copy counts), and a Repair Kit at the bench takes one off again
  (the part comes back at its quality). Perks never sit in a normal mod slot: no installable_tags, on purpose.

  HOW TO MAKE A SCALED PERK (stat perks - damage, magazine, reload, ...)
    Give the passive_effect two values and tier="1,90": the game slides smoothly between them by the part's quality.
      <passive_effect name="EntityDamage" operation="perc_add" value=".15,.35" tier="1,90"/>   Q1 = +15%, Q90 = +35%
    More points work too (tier="1,45,90" value="a,b,c").

  HOW TO MAKE A BANDED PERK (on-hit / on-kill effects - triggered_effect has no tier)
    Write one triggered_effect per quality band and add this requirement to each (Undead Legacy's bands shown):
      <requirement name="ArmoryUnbound.AuPerkQuality, ArmoryUnbound" min="1"  max="20"/>
      ... min="21" max="40" / min="41" max="60" / min="61" max="80" / min="81" max="90"
    The requirement is true only while that perk's own effects run, for the quality of THAT perk (two copies of one perk
    on a gun each use their own quality). Chance-based effects add RandomRoll as before.

  HOW TO MAKE A CORRUPTED PERK
    modifier_tags="auPerk,auCorrupted": shown in red. Give it an upside that grows (value="low,high") and a drawback that
    shrinks (value="-big,-small") with tier="1,90". Its part goes in loot only (see items.xml / the UL add-on's loot.xml).

  KIND TAGS (1.1.0): add auGunOnly to a perk that only works on guns (magazine, reload, fire rate, recoil) - the bench and console refuse it on melee weapons and tools; add auMagPerk to a magazine-size perk - also refused on bows. Everything else works on every kind.

  ADDING YOUR OWN PERK: copy a block, give it a new name, keep the tags, add "<name>" and "<name>Desc" to Localization.txt,
  and make a part for it in items.xml (property AuPerk = the perk name). No code needed.
  Hit effects only apply to targets tagged zombie or animal. Numbers are plain XML - tune them here.
-->
